{'symbol': 'ROP', 'date': '2021-10-03 00:01:00', 'title': 'ROPER TECHNOLOGIES TO SELL TRANSCORE FOR $2.68 BILLION', 'text': 'SARASOTA, FLA., OCT. 03, 2021 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- ROPER TECHNOLOGIES, INC. (NYSE: ROP), A LEADING DIVERSIFIED TECHNOLOGY COMPANY, TODAY ANNOUNCED THAT IT HAS REACHED A DEFINITIVE AGREEMENT TO DIVEST ITS TRANSCORE BUSINESS TO SINGAPORE TECHNOLOGIES ENGINEERING LTD (“ST ENGINEERING”), A GLOBAL TECHNOLOGY, DEFENSE, AND ENGINEERING GROUP, FOR $2.68 BILLION IN CASH. TRANSCORE IS EXPECTED TO GENERATE APPROXIMATELY $545 MILLION OF REVENUE AND $135 MILLION OF EBITDA IN 2021. ROPER WILL RETAIN ITS DAT AND LOADLINK NETWORK SOFTWARE BUSINESSES, WHICH IT ACQUIRED TOGETHER WITH TRANSCORE IN 2004.'}